 The function should use a for loop to iterate over the array and compare each element to the current largest number. If the current element is larger, it should be updated to be the new largest number. The function should return the largest number when it is finished iterating over the array.

Solution:
function largestNumber(arr) {
  let largest = arr[0];
  for (let i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] > largest) {
      largest = arr[i];
    }
  }
  return largest;
}
